---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · TachyonCMS"
  description="What tachyoncms.com keeps about you: your email address if you sign up and confirm, and nothing else. No analytics, no cookies."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Your email address, if you give it. That's all."
    lede="No analytics, no cookies, no tracking pixels, no ad scripts. Here's what does happen, piece by piece."
  >
    <p class="notice">Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-28">28 October 2026</time>.</p>
  </PageHero>

  <div class="privacy">
    <Prose split>
      <h2>Reading the site</h2>
      <p>
        Reading these pages sets no cookies and runs no analytics. The fonts and scripts come from tachyoncms.com itself,
        not from anyone else's servers, apart from the signup check described below.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site keeps nothing in your browser's local storage. The docs at docs.tachyoncms.com keep a few small layout
        choices in your browser, such as which sidebar sections are open, and those never leave your machine.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any host, Cloudflare handles your IP address and the usual request details
        to serve each page. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Signing up for email</h2>
      <p>The signup forms ask for one thing: your email address. Here's what happens to it.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>A check that you're a person.</strong> When you start on a form, the page loads Cloudflare Turnstile,
          and not before. Turnstile looks at signals from your browser to decide you aren't a bot, under{' '}
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/">Cloudflare's Turnstile privacy addendum</a>. When
          you submit, our server sends Cloudflare Turnstile's answer and your IP address to confirm it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A confirmation email.</strong> We send it through <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy"
            >Resend</a
          >, which keeps a record of the emails it sends, as mail services do. The link inside carries your address,
          signed so nobody else can confirm it for you, and it expires after 48 hours. Until you click it, your address
          isn't on any list, and our code never writes it to a log.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Confirmed.</strong> Once you click, your address is saved as a contact in Resend, in the one list every
          signup form joins. We use it only to write when there's a release or news of the admin.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Nothing else goes with it: no name, no location, no record of which pages you read. We don't sell the list or
        hand it to anyone. Resend holds it for us, and that's all.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting off the list</h2>
      <p>
        Two ways, whichever is closer to hand. Use the unsubscribe link at the bottom of any update we send. Or write
        to <a href="mailto:hello@tachyoncms.com">hello@tachyoncms.com</a> from the address you signed up with, and I'll
        delete it from Resend. That address also works for asking what we hold about you, which is at most your email
        address and when you confirmed it.
      </p>

      <h2>If this changes</h2>
      <p>
        This page will say so before the site changes. Its history is public, in the{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/tachyon-cms/website/commits/main/src/pages/privacy.astro">website's repository</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding: 64px 0 clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }
  .privacy :global(.prose > h2:first-child) {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
